# ---------------------------------------------------------------- IR (P23)
# Clone executes quest.ir blocks as IR; master emulates; absent blocks
# emulate (always safe). Requires -lockstep. Emit first, then launch with
# the envs — the loader hard-binds the IR to the exact CFG via sha256 and
# REFUSES on any mismatch, bad grammar, or book/stock mode mixups.
#
# Emit (stock mode — valid with or without the M4 book):
#   python3 tools/lower.py --dis <Disassembled>/quest.dis \
#     --blocks quest.blocks.split --pushmap quest.pushmap.M4 \
#     --argmap <Disassembled>/quest.argmap --all --out quest.ir2.stock
# Emit (book mode — decorated calls/argpushes lowered; book runs ONLY):
#   ... same, plus --book, --out quest.ir2.book
#
# Launch (book mode; this is the P23 gate configuration):
QUEST_BLOCKS=quest.blocks.split QUEST_SYNC_LIST=quest.synclist.split \
QUEST_SYNC_K=1 QUEST_IR=quest.ir2.book \
QUEST_ADDRESS_BOOK=quest.addrbook QUEST_PUSH_MAP=quest.pushmap.M4 \
./emulator -lockstep -silent ../../QUEST QUEST_SERVER @QUEST @QUEST >log
#
# Stock-mode IR: use QUEST_IR=quest.ir2.stock and (optionally) drop the
# ADDRESS_BOOK/PUSH_MAP envs. Book-mode IR without those envs is refused.
# NOTE the split CFG pair: quest.ir provenance is stamped against
# quest.blocks.split — QUEST_BLOCKS/QUEST_SYNC_LIST must be the .split
# files, not the originals, or the loader refuses at startup.
#
# Evidence on stderr: "IRExec: loaded N IR blocks" at start; one
# "first execution of block X" line per block (coverage).
# QUEST_IR_DEBUG_BLOCK=<hex8> prints per-statement ac state for a block.
# Combining with -handler=native / -zero=clone is expected to compose
# (IR dispatch sits inside the emulated fetch path) but the validated
# gate config is exactly the line above. Spec: docs/IR.md.
